# Exaai environment
# PostgreSQL via Supabase (pooled). Use the pooled connection string from
# the Supabase dashboard (Database → Connect → Transaction pooler) for
# Vercel/serverless functions.
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.PROJECT_REF:password@aws-0-eu-central-1.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true"

# Auth
SESSION_COOKIE_NAME="exai_session"
SESSION_TTL_DAYS=30

# Operators (US-030): comma-separated emails granted admin access to /ops
# ADMIN_EMAILS="you@example.com"

# Public base URL used in account emails (password reset links)
# APP_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# Generation provider: "mock" (default, offline, no API key) | "groq" (recommended) | "openai"
# | "openrouter" | "nvidia"
#
# LEAVE THIS UNSET to use the measured default chain in `src/lib/generate/chain.ts`
# (groq/openai/gpt-oss-120b then nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b). A provider key
# alone is enough to go live; AI_PROVIDER only pins ONE provider and bypasses the
# chain. AI_PROVIDER=mock is the exception — it always wins, and the test suite
# relies on that to stay offline.
#
# Measured live 2026-10-26, one passage request each:
#   groq:openai/gpt-oss-120b                   142 words / 3 paragraphs, 2.1s
#   nvidia:nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b   164 and 147 words / 3 paragraphs
#   nvidia:nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b  43 words / 1 paragraph, every run
#   openrouter:*                               403 "Key limit exceeded" (key over budget)
#   groq:gpt-oss-20b / qwen3.8-27b / allam-2-7b    403 blocked at the project level
#
# A validation failure is not fatal: the same entry gets ONE corrective call
# carrying the validator's own words, then the next entry is tried. That is why
# one mediocre model no longer fails a whole exam.
#
# Regardless of what you set here, Nemotron entries get
# `chat_template_kwargs.enable_thinking: false` on NVIDIA and
# `reasoning.enabled: false` on OpenRouter: left on, the reasoning trace consumes
# the whole max_tokens budget and the call returns empty content. gpt-oss gets a
# `reasoning_effort: low` cap for the same reason.
#
# Optional: GROQ_BASE_URL, OPENROUTER_BASE_URL, NVIDIA_BASE_URL override the
# default endpoints (useful for a proxy or a self-hosted OpenAI-compatible).
# AI_RUN_BUDGET_MS overrides the 120s ceiling on one full-exam run.
# AI_PROVIDER_CHAIN="groq:openai/gpt-oss-120b,nvidia:nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b"

# SMTP (production only — fail-closed if SMTP_HOST is missing)
# SMTP_HOST="smtp.example.com"
# SMTP_PORT="587"
# SMTP_SECURE="false"   # true/false; default true when port=465
# SMTP_USER=""
# SMTP_PASS=""
# SMTP_FROM="Exaai <no-reply@exaai.app>"

# Used when AI_PROVIDER="openai"
# OPENAI_API_KEY=""
# OPENAI_MODEL="gpt-4o-mini"
# OPENAI_BASE_URL="https://api.openai.com/v1"   # any OpenAI-compatible endpoint

# Used when AI_PROVIDER="groq"
# GROQ_API_KEY=""
# GROQ_MODEL="openai/gpt-oss-120b"
# GROQ_BASE_URL="https://api.groq.com/openai/v1"

# Fallback providers (keys only; models come from AI_PROVIDER_CHAIN above)
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=""
# NVIDIA_API_KEY=""

# Privacy note: free-tier endpoints may retain or train on prompts. Exam content
# is not sensitive, so this is accepted — recorded here so it stays a decision
# rather than an oversight.
